This process uses two JavaScript scripts executed via mongosh on a MongoDB server to:

Count documents in collections (excluding system DBs).

Fetch the database size on disk.

Log the results to .log files for validation or reporting.

### 1. Run collection count script
mongosh --port 57017 -u username -p  password PostvalidationCount.js >> /tmp/Collection_cmf-cluster1-dc2-de1.westus2.cloudapp.azure.com_57018_07_28_2025_10_06_15.log

### 2. Run DB size check script
mongosh --port 57017 -u username -p  password  PostvalidationDbsize.js >> /tmp/Size_cmf-cluster1-dc2-de1.westus2.cloudapp.azure.com_57018_07_28_2025_10_06_15.log

# 3. Review the results
Compare the source and target files to see the diff if any.

